] The important part of this example is the r array, which indicates that path entry 1 in the q array is the canonical path for item 0. That is, crate_name::Data has a canonical path of crate_name::submodule::Data. This might sound like a strange design, since it has the duplicate data. It's done that way because inlining can happen across crates, which are compiled separately and might not all be present in the docs. [ [ "crate_name", ... ], [ "crate_name_2", { "q": [[0, "crate_name::submodule"], [5, "core::option"]], ... }]
