Every function definition has a corresponding ZST that implements the Fn* traits known as a function item type . This part of the chapter will talk a little bit about the "desugaring" of function item types as it is useful context for explaining the difference between early bound and late bound generic parameters. Let's start with a very trivial example involving no generic parameters: fn foo(a: String) -> u8 { # 1 /* snip */
